# ---------------------------------------------------------------- personal data
# The raw export and anything derived from it that still carries free text or
# respondent IDs stays out of git. It contains a named professor, profanity, and
# per-respondent identifiers. This repo may become public when the page ships.
#
# The whole Docs/ folder is internal: it holds the raw export, and PROJECT.md section 5
# quotes the profanity from a review verbatim as evidence of the moderation problem.
# Correct in a planning doc, wrong in a repo that may go public. Delete this line if you
# decide the repo stays private and you want the spec versioned.
Docs/
data/reviews.csv
data/moderation_review.md

# The banned-pattern list names the faculty it checks for. Holding the name is the
# only way to prove the name never ships, but a public file listing surnames under
# the heading "banned" is the harm the moderation pass exists to prevent. Clone and
# copy banned_patterns.example.txt over it to run the pipeline yourself.
data/banned_patterns.txt

# Internal audit artifacts. Both key on per-respondent submission ids, and the
# moderation sheet carries the free text decisions. They are what the team signs
# off against; they are not part of what gets published.
data/moderation.csv
data/audit.md

# Committed instead: build/*.py (the pipeline), the published aggregates
# (oe_public.json, oe_stats.json, cards.json), the name and basket maps, the built
# index.html and the share cards. Re-run build/clean.py against the raw sheet to
# regenerate everything ignored above.

